v 3
d 'HMDBIVPOIS': module to fit hidden Markov bivariate Poisson regression with informative dropout
d
d hmdbivpois fits the hidden Markov dropout bivariate Poisson model of
d Carrieri, Gyrd-Hansen and Li Donni (2026, Journal of the Royal Statistical
d Society Series A) to two counts observed on the same individuals over time
d when individuals may leave the panel (for example by death) and the dropout
d is informative. A latent state that follows a first-order Markov chain and
d a time-constant latent class shift the means of the two counts (bivariate
d Poisson of the Famoye form) and the logit of the dropout. Estimation is by
d the EM algorithm with scaled forward-backward recursions, followed by direct
d maximization if needed. Options: multiple starting values, transitions
d with covariates, transformations of the lagged counts, current counts in the
d dropout equation, classes in selected equations, state-specific slopes.
d Postestimation: predict and estat (ic, transition, ame, survival, fit,
d lrtrans, stability).
d
d KW: hidden Markov
d KW: latent Markov
d KW: bivariate Poisson
d KW: informative dropout
d KW: count data
d KW: panel data
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Author: Paolo Li Donni
d Support: https://github.com/plidonni/hmdbivpois
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261118
d
f hmdbivpois.ado
f hmdbivpois_p.ado
